[I] The marriage of Apache and Perl

[T] mod_perl gives you a persistent Perl interpreter embedded in your
[T] web server. This lets you avoid the overhead of starting an
[T] external interpreter and avoids the penalty of Perl start-up time,
[T] giving you super-fast dynamic content.

[U] https://perl.apache.org/

[A] Per Einar Ellefsen <pereinar@oslo.online.no>
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

[C] extra/development

[L] APL
[V] 2.0.14

[D] f629e4b21e38406cba5a4bc4a06cde6fbbc7088c01baf3c041a9c485 mod_perl-2.0.14.tar.gz https://apache.org/dist/perl/

plconfopt="MP_APXS=$root/opt/apache/sbin/apxs"
